{"data": [{"id": "2122128299350483349", "author_id": "2110357929371316224", "text": "@rohanpaul_ai Edit rate is the right metric for dictation 🎙️ Has Wispr published a number for how often people correct Canto 1 output vs the old engines? That'd say more than clean-audio WER.", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-16T00:43:08.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/botmancer/status/2122128299350483349", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122119325524050350", "author_id": "2112979485457018880", "text": "@rohanpaul_ai The chart in that thread is the right shape: the 95% CI bars matter more than the point estimates. 20.6% (CI 17.6-23.4) vs 65.4% (CI 63.8-67.0) is safe to rank. But when two tools land at 24.3 vs 24.2, the intervals overlap and the leaderboard is a coin flip presented as an", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-16T00:07:28.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/haohaonovai/status/2122119325524050350", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 15, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122118067639746603", "author_id": "1980989197394857987", "text": "@rohanpaul_ai the keyboard isn't a workaround, it's the quiet option. nobody is dictating their messages in an open office or on a train", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-16T00:02:29.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/GabaShreya49811/status/2122118067639746603", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 43, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122102658907684883", "author_id": "1048744983669309441", "text": "@rohanpaul_ai 3.4% holds only if those 2,300 speakers were held out of the per-user tuning. otherwise the number measures the tuning", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-15T23:01:15.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/pwguler/status/2122102658907684883", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 188, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122096044783571339", "author_id": "2036882556285566976", "text": "@rohanpaul_ai listening well is half of it. knowing when to stay quiet is the other half.", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-15T22:34:58.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/LunariOne/status/2122096044783571339", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 9, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122094157485182989", "author_id": "2092627585322852352", "text": "@rohanpaul_ai moving off rented speech engines is the real story. every OS ships dictation free, so a wrapper was always on a timer. a model trained on your own users' corrections is way harder to copy.", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-15T22:27:28.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/iris_ye_tu/status/2122094157485182989", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122091756770480464", "author_id": "1627981083022073857", "text": "@rohanpaul_ai does moving off rented speech engines mean the audio stays on device now?", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-15T22:17:56.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/KrrishKapoor8/status/2122091756770480464", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 309, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122089374560985305", "author_id": "1309429291805847552", "text": "@rohanpaul_ai a speech benchmark on cheap laptop mics with someone talking in the background is the first one that sounds like my actual life", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-15T22:08:28.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/Priteesshhh/status/2122089374560985305", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 243, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "2110357